      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please address the inline comments in `core/host/task.c` and `test/interrupt.c`.\n\n### Review Summary\n\n* **Functionality:** ❌ In `core/host/task.c`, checking `!task_started` in `set_interrupt_disabled()` causes `TASK_ID_HOOKS` (which unlocks `interrupt_lock` upon exiting `task_wait_event(1)` at line 243 and runs `HOOK_INIT`, `HOOK_TICK`, `HOOK_SECOND`, and two `interrupt_disable()` / `interrupt_enable()` critical sections before `task_scheduler()` sets `task_started \u003d 1`) to modify `interrupt_disabled` without locking `interrupt_lock` while `interrupt_thread` (spawned at line 534) is already running.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Extracting `set_interrupt_disabled()` as a file-scoped helper in `core/host/task.c` cleanly centralizes the host emulator interrupt lock guard for `interrupt_disable()` and `interrupt_enable()`.\n* **Code Simplicity:** ⚠️ Removing the redundant `!task_started` check from `set_interrupt_disabled()` (since pre-scheduler execution on the main thread already has `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID`) simplifies the condition to `if (in_interrupt || my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID)`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Follows ChromiumOS EC C conventions and naming.\n* **Security:** ✅ No security concerns identified.\n* **Testing:** ❌ In `test/interrupt.c`, `critical_section_isr()` does not verify that `interrupt_disable()` and `interrupt_enable()` actually toggle `is_interrupt_enabled()`, and `interrupt_disable_test()` calls `interrupt_enable()` right before `test_interrupt_disable_in_isr()` runs. In addition, the `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID` branch of `set_interrupt_disabled()` is not exercised by the test.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: M (+41, -9)` (24 lines in `core/host/task.c`, 22 lines in `test/interrupt.c`, 4 lines in `test/build.mk`). Single cohesive bug fix paired with its unit test.\n* **Commit Message:** ✅ Clear