      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `!task_started` should be removed from this guard:\n\n1. **`task_start()` does not hold `interrupt_lock` while `TASK_ID_HOOKS` initializes:** In `task_start()` (lines 532–541), `interrupt_lock` is locked while `TASK_ID_HOOKS` is parked inside `task_wait_event(1)` (line 478). As soon as `task_start()` signals `tasks[TASK_ID_HOOKS].resume`, `TASK_ID_HOOKS` wakes up at line 239 and unlocks `interrupt_lock` at line 243 before returning from `task_wait_event(1)` and invoking `hook_task()`.\n2. **Skipping `interrupt_lock` when `!task_started` races with `interrupt_thread` during `hook_task()` initialization:** `task_start()` spawns `interrupt_thread` at line 534 *before* resuming `TASK_ID_HOOKS` at line 541, while `task_started` is not set to `1` until `task_scheduler()` starts at line 439. During that window, `hook_task()` runs `HOOK_INIT`, `HOOK_TICK`, `HOOK_SECOND`, and two `interrupt_disable()` / `interrupt_enable()` critical sections (`common/hooks.c` lines 183–247). With `!task_started` in the condition, `TASK_ID_HOOKS` (`my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_HOOKS`) updates `interrupt_disabled` without holding `interrupt_lock` while `interrupt_thread` is already running and reading `interrupt_disabled` under `interrupt_lock` in `task_trigger_test_interrupt()`.\n3. **Pre-scheduler calls on the main thread are already covered:** Any call before `task_start()` (e.g., in `test_main()` or `HOOK_INIT_EARLY`) or inside `task_start()` / `task_scheduler()` executes on the main thread, where `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID` is already true.\n\n```c\n/*\n * Only lock interrupt_lock from task or interrupt-generator threads. In an ISR\n * (task_trigger_test_interrupt() holds it) or on the main/scheduler thread\n * (my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID, where a sleeping task may hold it), locking\n * it here would deadlock.\n */\nstatic void set_interrupt_disabled(int disabled)\n{\n\tif (in_interrupt || my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID) {\n\t\tinterrupt_disabled \u003d disabled;\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\tpthread_mutex_lock(\u0026interrupt_lock);\n\tinterrupt_disabled \u003d disabled;\n\tpthread_mutex_unlock(\u0026interrupt_lock);\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/d1b82277-a56b-4537-9524-1e9ebfe27e69)",
