      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Strengthen this test to verify both the interrupt state transitions inside the ISR and the `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID` branch of `set_interrupt_disabled()`:\n\n1. **Verify `is_interrupt_enabled()` inside `critical_section_isr()` (lines **34–39**):** Currently, `critical_section_isr()` never checks that `interrupt_disable()` actually disabled interrupts (`!is_interrupt_enabled()`), and because `interrupt_disable_test()` runs immediately before `test_interrupt_disable_in_isr()` and calls `interrupt_enable()` from task context at line 86, `TEST_ASSERT(is_interrupt_enabled())` here would still pass even if `critical_section_isr()` ran once during `interrupt_test()` and failed to re-enable interrupts (or if `set_interrupt_disabled()` returned early on `in_interrupt` without updating `interrupt_disabled`).\n2. **Exercise the `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID` branch:** During `interrupt`, `interrupt_disable()` and `interrupt_enable()` are only called from `TASK_ID_HOOKS`, `TASK_ID_TEST_RUNNER`, and `critical_section_isr()` (`in_interrupt \u003d\u003d true`), leaving `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID` untested. Toggling `interrupt_disable()` / `interrupt_enable()` in `test_init()` (which `test_main()` runs on the main thread where `my_task_id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_INVALID`) covers that branch as well.\n\n```c\n/* ISRs may enter a critical section with interrupt_disable(). */\nstatic void critical_section_isr(void)\n{\n\tinterrupt_disable();\n\tif (is_interrupt_enabled())\n\t\thas_error \u003d 1;\n\tcritical_section_isr_count++;\n\tinterrupt_enable();\n\tif (!is_interrupt_enabled())\n\t\thas_error \u003d 1;\n}\n```\n\n```c\nvoid test_init(void)\n{\n\tinterrupt_disable();\n\tif (is_interrupt_enabled())\n\t\thas_error \u003d 1;\n\tinterrupt_enable();\n\tif (!is_interrupt_enabled())\n\t\thas_error \u003d 1;\n}\n\nstatic int test_interrupt_disable_in_isr(void)\n{\n\tTEST_GT(critical_section_isr_count, 0, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_ASSERT(!has_error);\n\tTEST_ASSERT(is_interrupt_enabled());\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/d1b82277-a56b-4537-9524-1e9ebfe27e69)",
